    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, the PREMIS suggestion is really helpful. One more thing—when we deal with maps that have these really strange, unidentifiable symbols or markings that don't correspond to any known cartographic notations, how do we document those? We don't want to ignore them because they might be important for future analysis, but we also don't have a way to categorize them within standard geographic or historical taxonomies. Is there a way to record these \"unexplained\" elements without making the metadata look speculative or unscientific?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
