      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Documenting unexplained symbols requires a precise, descriptive approach within the metadata. Use the `dc:description` element to provide a literal, objective description of the symbol, detailing its appearance, placement, and context on the map. You can also employ `dc:subject` tags to list broad, descriptive terms like \"Unidentified Cartographic Symbols\" or \"Obscure Notation,\" signaling the element's nature without forcing it into a rigid taxonomy. This preserves the visual evidence for future experts to investigate.",
